It is compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and written beside the
executable on first start, so that a deploy stays a single file. It runs
both models above; it replaced tract, which produced identical scores but
took twelve times as long per forward pass on the deployment hardware.

The photo-advertisement lock uses Tesseract 5.3.4 with Leptonica 1.82.0
and the official `fas` and `eng` language data. The executable, its direct
native libraries, and tessdata are compiled into the release binary. On
first use they are integrity-checked and published to a content-addressed
directory beside the executable; nothing is downloaded at runtime and no
shell is used. The remaining shared libraries are supplied by the declared
Ubuntu service host.

The pinned files came from Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble) binary packages. Tesseract,
Leptonica and tessdata carry Apache License 2.0 terms. libarchive carries
the BSD 2-Clause license, giflib carries its MIT-style license, and libxml2
and ICU carry MIT licenses. Upstream copyright texts retained by the packages
