clip.onnx is the vision tower of CLIP ViT-B/32, licensed under the MIT
License.

    Source:  https://github.com/openai/CLIP
    Weights: https://huggingface.co/openai/clip-vit-base-patch32
    ONNX:    https://huggingface.co/Xenova/clip-vit-base-patch32

It is the one model that is not part of this repository: at 335 MB it is
loaded from a file of that name beside the executable, because embedding it
makes rustc materialise the whole array into the object file and the link
needs several gigabytes. It is used only by the topic locks, to turn a
thumbnail into a 512-value embedding. It takes RGB
[1, 3, 224, 224] normalised with CLIP's own mean and standard deviation
and emits image_embeds directly. Only the vision tower ships; the text
tower was run once, offline, to produce the concept vectors in
src/handlers/concept_vectors.rs and is not part of this program.
